### AI Engineering Lab - HTTP requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client)
### Postman users: import postman/ai-engineering-lab.postman_collection.json

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Generate an embedding (nothing is stored)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/embeddings
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "Employees are entitled to 12 casual leave days per year."}

### 2. Same meaning vs. different meaning
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/embeddings/similarity
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "texts": [
    "Employees receive 12 casual leave days every year.",
    "Workers are entitled to twelve days of casual leave annually.",
    "Spring Boot provides dependency injection."
  ]
}

### 3. Insert a document
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/documents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "hr-emergency-leave-example",
  "text": "Employees can take up to 5 days of emergency leave.",
  "metadata": {"department": "HR", "documentType": "POLICY", "source": "employee-handbook"}
}

### 4. Read it back, including the vector stored in pgvector
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/documents/hr-emergency-leave-example?includeEmbedding=true

### 5. Load the 30-document sample dataset
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/documents/batch
Content-Type: application/json

< ../../02-vector-databases/dataset/documents.json

### 6. Semantic search
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/search
Content-Type: application/json

{"query": "How many emergency leave days can an employee take?", "topK": 5}

### 7. Semantic search with a metadata filter
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/search
Content-Type: application/json

{"query": "How much time off do I get when a close relative passes away?", "topK": 3, "filterExpression": "department == 'HR'"}

### 8. Model and vector table in use
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/info
